# Open-source repo — no deployment-specific config

This repository is **open source**. Treat everything that lands in git as public.

## Never commit

- Secrets, tokens, passwords, private keys, service accounts
- Environment- or deployment-specific values (real DSNs, production URLs wired as hardcodes, upload keystores, Play/App Store credentials)
- Machine-local paths or personal machine config

## Do instead

- Load deploy-specific values from **gitignored** files (`android/local.properties`, `ios/Config.xcconfig`, `keystore.properties`) or **CI/env secrets** (`SENTRY_DSN`, `KEYSTORE_*`, etc.)
- Keep **examples only** in git (`*.example`, docs placeholders, empty `sentry.dsn=`)
- Prefer `BuildConfig` / env injection over hardcoding in source

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded deploy config in source
options.dsn = "https://abc@o123.ingest.sentry.io/456"

// ✅ GOOD — from gitignored local.properties / env → BuildConfig
options.dsn = BuildConfig.SENTRY_DSN  // empty ⇒ feature disabled
```

```properties
# ✅ local.properties (gitignored)
sdk.dir=/Users/YOU/Library/Android/sdk
sentry.dsn=https://…@….ingest.sentry.io/…
```

If a change needs a real production value to run locally, put it in a gitignored file and document the key name in `docs/` or `*.example` — never paste the live value into tracked source.
